<section class="section article-section" id="accounts"><div class="section-heading"><span class="section-index">02 / ACCOUNTS</span><h2>International accounts and getting paid</h2></div><p>In <strong>nsave</strong>, account balances can be held in multiple currencies. Open <strong>Account Details</strong> to inspect the USD account. ACH details include a routing number and account number; these are different from <strong>SWIFT / international wire</strong> details used for some cross-border payments.</p><div class="info-grid"><div><h3>USD ACH details</h3><p>nsave lists USD ACH account details and receiving USD transfers without a receiving fee from nsave. Confirm the sending platform accepts your details and country.</p></div><div><h3>Wire / SWIFT details</h3><p>A separate international wire account may need activation. The free plan lists $5.99 setup and $0.99 monthly for applicable wire accounts; paid plans can include some of these accounts.</p></div><div><h3>EUR and GBP accounts</h3><p>Euro and sterling account availability depends on your country and subscription. Distinguish account activation fees from FX and outbound payment fees.</p></div></div><p>Freelancers may be able to receive client or employer payments from providers such as Upwork or Fiverr, depending on platform withdrawal rules. The tutorial also covers a practical workflow for building an invoice with client details, line items, amounts and taxes, then sharing the payment link or bank details.</p><p class="footnote">An invoice link is not necessarily a full card-processing checkout; the customer must use a supported settlement method.</p></section>
<section class="section article-section" id="card"><div class="section-heading"><span class="section-index">03 / VISA</span><h2>Visa virtual card: issuance and usage</h2></div><p>The <strong>nsave Visa Platinum</strong> is a virtual USD-denominated card requested from the <strong>Cards</strong> tab. A complete billing address, up-to-date application and sufficient balance may be required; the issuing partner reviews eligibility.</p><ol class="steps"><li>Open the <strong>Cards</strong> section and request a new card.</li><li>Select <strong>Visa Platinum</strong> and review the current issuance fee for your plan.</li><li>Verify your legal name, street, postal code and region, then accept the issuer terms.</li><li>Once approved, view card number, expiration date and CVV in the app.</li><li>Use card controls to freeze or unfreeze it as appropriate, keeping recurring subscription payments in mind.</li></ol><div class="notice"><strong>USD spending fees:</strong> nsave's pricing page lists <strong>no nsave card transaction fee for USD spending</strong>. Paying in a currency different from the card account currency may incur <strong>1.5%</strong>. Card issuance itself may cost <strong>$1.99</strong> on Essential; Platinum is included with qualifying paid plans.</div><p>The actual payment demonstrated in the video was a <strong>successful Google Play game purchase</strong>. The tutorial does not show a completed, confirmed direct ChatGPT or Claude subscription payment.</p></section>
<section class="section article-section" id="plans"><div class="section-heading"><span class="section-index">04 / PRICING</span><h2>Plans and pricing explained</h2></div><p>The table below summarizes published personal-plan pricing at the time of review. Actual availability can vary by country. Distinguish recurring <strong>membership costs</strong> from optional account activation charges and transfer fees.</p><div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Plans"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Feature</th><th scope="col">Essential</th><th scope="col">Pro</th><th scope="col">Prestige</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Monthly fee</th><td>$0</td><td>$5.99</td><td>$29.99</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Visa Platinum issuance</th><td>$1.99</td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Visa Infinite card</th><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>✓</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">USD / EUR / GBP conversion</th><td>1%</td><td>0.5%</td><td>0.5%</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">USD / EUR wire accounts</th><td>$5.99 + $0.99/mo</td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">GBP wire account</th><td>$5.99 + $0.99/mo</td><td>$5.99 + $0.99/mo</td><td>✓</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">General card cashback</th><td>—</td><td>0.5%</td><td>1% up to $5k/mo, then 0.5%</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3>Common transaction fees</h3><div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Transaction fees"><table><thead><tr><th>Transaction</th><th>Reference fee</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">USD card payment from USD balance</th><td>0$</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Card spending in another currency</th><td>1.5%</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Receiving USD ACH / SWIFT transfers</th><td>0$ (nsave)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Sending USD via ACH</th><td>$0.50</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Sending USD via SWIFT</th><td>$12.99</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Sending GBP via FPS</th><td>$1</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Sending EUR via SEPA</th><td>$1</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Sending stablecoins to external wallet</th><td>1%</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">USD payout to Egyptian bank</th><td>$3.50</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">EGP local payout</th><td>≥ $1 (see in-app quote)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="footnote">Fees and features can change. Your current in-app confirmation screen and official documents take precedence.</p></section>
<section class="section article-section" id="deposit"><div class="section-heading"><span class="section-index">05 / FUNDING</span><h2>Funding nsave with Bybit and stablecoins</h2></div><p>The video shows a <strong>Bybit → nsave</strong> stablecoin transfer using <strong>USDC on Polygon</strong> via nsave's web portal. This is not a universal setup: the web-portal method is documented for users who previously had access, while nsave's current <strong>in-app deposit flow</strong> supports <strong>USDC and USDT on Solana</strong>, with a documented <strong>$1 minimum</strong> for that route. Always use the exact network displayed in your own nsave deposit screen.</p><ol class="steps"><li>Go to <strong>Deposit</strong> and open the stablecoin option actually available to your account.</li><li>Choose the token and network, and read the displayed minimum deposit.</li><li>Copy the receiving address without retyping it, then open your sending exchange such as Bybit.</li><li>Choose an <strong>on-chain withdrawal</strong> and confirm the <strong>token, network and destination</strong> all match the nsave instructions.</li><li>Ensure the net amount after the sender's withdrawal fee meets the deposit minimum, then confirm and monitor transaction records and the blockchain explorer.</li></ol><div class="notice alert"><strong>Irreversible transaction risk:</strong> Sending the right token on the wrong chain — or to the wrong address — can permanently lose the funds. The network selected on the exchange must match the destination network shown by nsave.</div><p>Bank transfers, employers and eligible connected payment providers may offer other funding methods. Some received stablecoins are automatically credited as USD in the nsave account.</p></section>
<section class="section article-section" id="withdraw"><div class="section-heading"><span class="section-index">06 / PAYOUTS</span><h2>Withdrawals to Egypt and local accounts</h2></div><p>To make an Egypt payout, open <strong>Send</strong>, add a recipient, choose <strong>Egypt</strong> and the receiving currency, then select the supported payout rail. Official guidance documents <strong>bank transfer</strong>, <strong>InstaPay</strong> and mobile wallets such as Vodafone Cash or Orange Cash, subject to account eligibility.</p><ol class="steps"><li>Pick Egypt and the available receiving currency, usually EGP or sometimes USD.</li><li>Enter verified bank/SWIFT, InstaPay or wallet beneficiary details for the selected rail.</li><li>Enter the amount and review the current FX rate, fees and actual amount to be delivered.</li><li>Confirm the transfer purpose and final details, then track the payout status in transactions.</li></ol><p>The nsave Egypt help page states a <strong>$1 minimum fee</strong> for EGP payouts and a <strong>$3.50</strong> fee for sending USD to an Egyptian bank. Actual exchange rates and fees must be reviewed in-app at confirmation time.</p></section>
<section class="section article-section" id="ai"><div class="section-heading"><span class="section-index">07 / PAYMENTS</span><h2>Card payments, ChatGPT and Claude subscriptions</h2></div><p>If you want to pay for <strong>ChatGPT or Claude</strong>, the video explains nsave virtual Visa usage and the difference between a Google Play purchase and a direct website subscription. Not every merchant or country is guaranteed to accept the card; issuer, merchant and region policies control acceptance.</p><div class="info-grid"><div><h3>USD card spending</h3><p>Official pricing shows <strong>$0 nsave card transaction fees</strong> for payments billed in USD from the USD balance. This does not make subscriptions free.</p></div><div><h3>Limited AI cashback</h3><p>Official nsave promotion runs <strong>Oct 22–Nov 30, 2026</strong>: 50% cashback on the first eligible ChatGPT or Claude transaction, capped at <strong>$5</strong>, with a minimum qualifying charge of $3 and further conditions.</p></div><div><h3>Direct billing matters</h3><p>The AI cashback requires direct billing by OpenAI or Anthropic. Payments routed through <strong>Google Play or the App Store are excluded</strong> from this particular promotion.</p></div></div><p>Qualifying cashback may take up to 30 days after settlement. This time-limited offer can change or end early; read official terms before subscribing.</p></section>
<section class="section article-section" id="bonus"><div class="section-heading"><span class="section-index">08 / REWARDS</span><h2>Welcome reward: what to check before funding</h2></div><p>This guide uses the specific sign-up URL below. Under nsave's <strong>salary/coworker referral</strong> program, both people can receive <strong>$10</strong> after a new invitee signs up and deposits <strong>$150+</strong>. Other nsave referral programs may impose different funding and external-transfer requirements.</p><p>The original referral description mentions <strong>60 days</strong>, but we could not verify a 60-day deposit deadline for this exact URL. <strong>Read the offer terms on the referral page and in your account before depositing.</strong></p><div class="ref-box"><code dir="ltr">https://web.nsave.com/invite/khalifa_majid</code><a class="btn btn-red" href="https://web.nsave.com/invite/khalifa_majid" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer sponsored">Sign up for nsave ↗</a></div></section>
