<section class="section article-section" id="faq"><div class="section-heading"><span class="section-index">11 / FAQ</span><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2></div><div class="faqs"><details><summary>Are nsave USD card payments free of fees?</summary><p>nsave pricing lists no nsave transaction fee for USD card payments from the USD balance. Paying in another currency can incur 1.5%, and merchants may charge separately.</p></details><details><summary>Is the Visa Platinum card free for everyone?</summary><p>No. Essential pricing lists a one-time $1.99 fee; qualifying Pro/Prestige plans include Platinum. Some previous cardholders have separate exceptions.</p></details><details><summary>Can every account deposit USDC on Polygon?</summary><p>Do not assume so. The video uses a legacy web-portal flow; current in-app stablecoin deposits are documented for USDC and USDT on Solana. Follow your own deposit screen.</p></details><details><summary>Can I withdraw to InstaPay or Vodafone Cash?</summary><p>Official Egypt payout guidance includes bank accounts, InstaPay and supported mobile wallets, subject to account and payout eligibility.</p></details><details><summary>Did the tutorial prove ChatGPT subscription payments work?</summary><p>It proves a Google Play purchase succeeded in that demonstration; it does not show a completed direct ChatGPT or Claude subscription.</p></details><details><summary>How do I get the $10 welcome reward?</summary><p>nsave has multiple referral programs. Check this exact referral offer. One program describes new sign-ups and deposits of at least $150; qualification cannot be guaranteed.</p></details><details><summary>Is this the official nsave site?</summary><p>No. This is an independent guide published by Majd Fatihy, linking to official nsave support and pricing resources.</p></details></div></section>
